  "summary": "Sheinbaum says Sinaloa's interim governor should serve through October 2027. Sinaloa's Congress is due to name a replacement Monday after granting Rubén Rocha Moya a second indefinite leave. Rocha had returned to office for about a day and a half while facing a US criminal case.",
  "lead": {
    "h1": "Sheinbaum says Sinaloa's interim governor should serve through October 2027",
    "context": "Sinaloa's Congress is due to name a replacement Monday after granting Rubén Rocha Moya a second indefinite leave. Rocha had returned to office for about a day and a half while facing a US criminal case.",
    "background": "Sinaloa's constitution requires Congress to appoint an interim governor when an absence lasts more than 30 days. The appointment requires an absolute majority.",
    "view": "The second leave turns a brief return into a longer succession decision. If Congress appoints someone through October 2027, that person, not Rocha, will run the state while the US case proceeds.",
    "prediction": "Congress's appointment will show whether the handover lasts through October 2027. A shorter term would leave the succession open.",
